[ti:The Invisible Hand]
[ar:EdgarAllanMusic]
[al:1984s.text - Rectified]
[length:04:45.15]

[00:05.07]Records Department
[00:06.76]Another little cylinder... another little lie to correct
[00:11.52]Times, seventeen-three. Speech misreported. Rectify
[00:16.91]Relax, comrade. Nothing is lost... everything is corrected
[00:23.65]The draught is warm... like a hand on my back
[00:27.84]We are holding you
[00:31.18]...You never feel the hand
[00:34.88]Instrumental
[02:08.25]Creamy pages older than the war itself
[02:12.69]Bought in a junk shop off a dusty shelf
[02:16.02]To the future, to the past, in clumsy lines
[02:20.78]Every letter feels like crossing the line
[02:24.53]Your hand moves on its own across the page
[02:28.69]Down with big brother... written in a daze
[02:34.05]Thoughtcrime is death... thoughtcrime is death
[02:42.13]You're already dead with every single breath
[02:49.97]And the invisible hand that wipes the past
[02:58.97]Thoughtcrime is death... and it's coming fast
[03:05.95]By day you feed the memory hole
[03:10.16]A warm draught takes the paper whole
[03:13.96]We were always at war with the enemy of today
[03:18.65]Doublethink twists the knife and you look away
[03:22.56]A name you typed at nine is no one by ten
[03:26.42]Every record rewritten... it never was, again
[03:31.89]The hand that writes... the hand that wipes the past
[03:40.13]You're already dead with every single breath
[03:46.85]So soft, so warm, it holds you in its grasp
[03:56.84]Thoughtcrime is death... and it's coming fast
[04:05.48]Who holds the past holds what's to come
[04:10.13]Freedom is saying two and two make four
[04:15.82]Hold on to that... hold on to that
[04:21.14]The page is full... but you're already gone
[04:24.81]
